{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reconsider accepting the independent review of antisemitism in schools",
        "additional_details": "In our view, the review places one form of racism above others in a distinct hierarchy and that risks fracturing school frameworks and alienating other marginalized groups. We are concerned that separating antisemitism from overall anti-racism policies risks creating unequal protections and prejudice. In light of this review, we also call on DfE to clarify it impartiality rules to make sure pupils and teachers are fully allowed to show solidarity with Palestine.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to reconsider accepting the 27 recommendations of the independent review of antisemitism in schools. We think rules on antisemitism must stay part of overall anti-racism policies.",
